**How to implement.** The source slot's item is the run's source: it emits its own Stokes state times its intensity scale (001 §N 'The source is real: a source item with a Stokes state and an intensity scale'; the S8.1 mapper's request: the source slot's item emits through `emissionWith (ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters)`; step 252 (c): every chart reads the default parameter set until S8.2's source slot gives a source item's own values). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) On the model extension holding `tryItemModelChoice` (step 263): `member model.runEmission : Result<SourceEmission, ControlCaption>`, the error being the text the failure chart shows. For the first `LightSource` slot of the table holding an item whose `tryItemModelChoice` resolves, it is `choice.emissionWith (ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters)` (step 246), an `ItemEvaluationError` answering its `describe`; for such a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve, the `describe` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming it (step 255); and otherwise `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)`, step 252's default. (2) `chartForRun` reads every point with `model.runEmission` where it read the default emission, an `Error text` showing step 252's `The run cannot be evaluated` chart with that text. The wavelength stays the bound preset's (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:boundSource`), because a source item's slot is bound to its preset (step 258). Each doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. With no source item every chart is step 252's. Tests, in `ExperimentControlsTests`, over `initMain ()` whose source slot holds a `Laser` item of the HeNe preset (`AddItem`, `AssignSlot`), with one linear polarizer bound to its preset between it and the seeded intensity detector, varied over R1 0 … 180° in 7 points: `a source item emits its own polarization through the run`: with `degreeOfPolarization` 1 and `azimuth` 30° (`SetParameterState`, step 240) each S₀ is 1 + cos(2(x − 30°)) within 1e-12 (the polarizer is the intensity reference, r = 2, step 252), and with the item's defaults each S₀ is 1, as the default source reads. `a source item whose parameters the run cannot evaluate shows that the run cannot be evaluated`: with `degreeOfPolarization` set to 1.5 the chart's title is `The run cannot be evaluated` and its description names `degreeOfPolarization` (`ParameterOutOfRangeErr`, step 245). All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the source slot emits, `model.runEmission` MUST be the source item's emission through `emissionWith` over its own parameters, the default parameter set without one, and `chartForRun` MUST read with it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a source item emits its own polarization through the run` and `a source item whose parameters the run cannot evaluate shows that the run cannot be evaluated`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
